   1: # Mark of Kri / PS2Recomp Integration Contract
   2: 
   3: ## Reuse candidates
   4: 
   5: | Component | Initial decision |
   6: |---|---|
   7: | R5900 decoder | Reuse and verify |
   8: | CodeGenerator | Reuse through project adapter |
   9: | Function emitter | Reuse and verify generated ABI |
  10: | Control-flow analysis | Reuse and test against Mark evidence |
  11: | PS2Runtime | Reuse initially |
  12: | R5900Context | Reuse initially |
  13: | VU translators | Reuse, then validate |
  14: | MMI translators | Reuse, then validate |
  15: | COP0/COP1 translators | Reuse, then validate |
  16: | Memory helpers | Reuse, then validate |
  17: | Graphics frontend | Evaluate separately for native PC needs |
  18: 
  19: ## Known concerns
  20: 
  21: 1. Generated functions use PS2Runtime and R5900Context.
  22: 2. The upstream runtime contains platform-facing dependencies.
  23: 3. CodeGenerator exposes useful direct methods, but its input data
  24:    structures and generated-file integration still need a compiled test.
  25: 4. LQC2/SQC2 translation paths exist through LDC2/SDC2 aliases.
  26: 5. Translation paths do not prove complete PS2 hardware semantics.
  27: 
  28: ## First acceptance gate
  29: 
  30: A controlled test slice is accepted only when:
  31: 
  32: - generated C++ is deterministic;
  33: - generated code compiles;
  34: - the required runtime ABI links;
  35: - test execution produces expected state changes;
  36: - delay-slot behavior is tested independently;
  37: - failures and unsupported semantics are reported explicitly.
  38: 
  39: No full-game generation before this gate passes.

